WEBVTT

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.170
Master Kaoru, please explain.

00:00:05.570 --> 00:00:07.640
Don't you trust Master Kaoru?

00:00:11.670 --> 00:00:15.340
Master Kaoru, please don't tell them.

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:21.050
Master Kaoru.

00:00:21.320 --> 00:00:25.790
Wasn't it a secret just between the two of us from that day onward?

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:31.430
Nadeshiko, please don't tell anyone else about this.

00:00:32.530 --> 00:00:36.130
Don't worry.
I won't tell this to anybody else.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:37.970
Not a single soul.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:44.040
As promised, I never told anyone.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:48.940
Because it's a secret between the two of us that nobody else knows.

00:00:51.010 --> 00:00:54.080
I've caused trouble for everyone.

00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:55.650
Master Kaoru?

00:00:55.650 --> 00:00:57.090
I'll tell you everything.

00:00:57.350 --> 00:00:58.650
What are you...

00:00:59.660 --> 00:01:00.890
I'm...

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:04.730
Not the Kaoru Kawahira that you think.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:09.970
Master Kaoru.

00:01:15.770 --> 00:01:19.510
<i>Can I keep on praying?</i>

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:22.880
<i>Can I keep on believing?</i>

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:29.750
<i>Oh light that shines</i> <i>in the forest of despair</i>

00:01:40.330 --> 00:01:46.240
<i>I kick the cold ground with my toes</i>

00:01:47.000 --> 00:01:53.310
<i>My brushed hair</i> <i>dances in the moonlit night</i>

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:59.950
<i>Let's throw away your</i> <i>frightened eyes and loneliness</i>

00:02:00.380 --> 00:02:07.690
<i>Those days when acting tough</i> <i>was your only friend...</i>

00:02:07.690 --> 00:02:12.360
<i>Leave that in the distance</i>

00:02:12.360 --> 00:02:16.300
<i>Is my salvation over there?</i>

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.600
<i>Can I heal this deep darkness?</i>

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:25.270
<i>Is it okay for me to seek warmth?</i>

00:02:25.810 --> 00:02:29.550
<i>I want to be stronger</i> <i>than anyone else</i>

00:02:29.550 --> 00:02:32.850
<i>I want to protect my loved ones</i>

00:02:32.850 --> 00:02:38.990
<i>Oh light that continues</i> <i>to shine on me</i>

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.990
Kaoru and Nadeshiko!

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.100
Such a wonderful view.

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:53.870
The wind feels great on my crotch too.

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.440
By gaining Dai Yoko's power...

00:02:57.440 --> 00:03:00.880
Daisakkai's energy has maxed out.

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:04.510
Daisakkai is the collection of my magical power.

00:03:04.510 --> 00:03:07.880
By using that power,
I can grant any wish.

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:11.390
My wish is a world where everything is free.

00:03:11.390 --> 00:03:14.490
Principles, policies, ways of life...

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:18.490
A wonderful world with no limitations on such things.

00:03:18.490 --> 00:03:21.160
And that is no longer just a dream.

00:03:24.700 --> 00:03:27.400
That pervert mage is having his way.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:30.540
But to think he got ahold of Dai Yoko's power.

00:03:30.540 --> 00:03:33.340
Stay focused, Hake.
Stop him at all costs.

00:03:33.340 --> 00:03:34.280
Yes.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:39.420
Kaoru's secret?

00:03:39.850 --> 00:03:41.220
What's that?

00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:44.620
Master Kaoru isn't Master Kaoru?

00:03:44.620 --> 00:03:46.560
What does that mean?

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:48.820
What's that? I don't get it.

00:03:48.820 --> 00:03:50.060
Please explain.

00:03:50.060 --> 00:03:51.430
Master Kaoru!

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:55.530
That's right, I'm not the real Kaoru Kawahira.

00:03:55.530 --> 00:03:59.400
To be precise, this body isn't that of Kaoru Kawahira's.

00:04:00.640 --> 00:04:04.510
When I was a kid,
I was raised by a certain mage.

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:09.750
He taught me everything, and then took everything from me.

00:04:10.550 --> 00:04:12.010
Listen, Kaoru.

00:04:12.010 --> 00:04:16.750
The most important thing for people to live is love.

00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:18.150
Love?

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.720
He was a mage that had lived for over a thousand years.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:26.500
He lost his body from various magic experiments.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.660
But he kept living as a soul.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.930
He taught me many things.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.870
He was both a father and a teacher to me.

00:04:36.540 --> 00:04:39.940
He taught me how to study, play piano, and use magic.

00:04:42.650 --> 00:04:46.420
So when I learned that he used magic

00:04:46.420 --> 00:04:50.050
to help the sick and poor,
I was happy.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:53.090
I thought his job was to help people.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:55.160
At least for that time.

00:04:55.460 --> 00:04:59.090
After a while, he started dying.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:01.660
I wanted to do something.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:05.800
But it wasn't something medicine or magic could do.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:10.670
There was only one thing that gave him power.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:17.310
According to his explanation, there was a hunter that hated people.

00:05:17.750 --> 00:05:21.350
He didn't listen to anyone in the village and lived alone.

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:24.220
The villagers despised him back.

00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.560
That man was always alone.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:31.590
The mage went to that man and explained about people's love.

00:05:32.130 --> 00:05:34.700
He tried to make the man make up with the villagers.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:37.700
But the man didn't listen to a single thing.

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:42.710
But the mage never gave up and kept convincing him.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:49.680
It was then.

00:05:50.710 --> 00:05:53.720
The man fell from a cliff and was badly hurt.

00:05:57.990 --> 00:06:02.120
Not a single person helped the hated man.

00:06:02.460 --> 00:06:03.560
But...

00:06:35.020 --> 00:06:36.790
The man changed.

00:06:37.330 --> 00:06:39.090
He opened up to the villagers.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.500
As he worked seriously for the village,

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:46.000
the villagers started to accept that man.

00:06:46.670 --> 00:06:48.640
That man learned about love.

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:53.110
And a couple years later, he married the girl who saved him.

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:56.040
Oh my, Keita, are you hungry?

00:06:56.040 --> 00:06:57.450
Want some milk?

00:06:57.450 --> 00:06:59.580
You idiot. What are you doing?

00:07:01.450 --> 00:07:03.150
Listen to me seriously.

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:04.950
We are.

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:06.920
That mage is a pretty good guy.

00:07:07.660 --> 00:07:10.090
No, there's still more to it.

00:07:10.090 --> 00:07:12.730
It was all a carefully crafted plan.

00:07:13.260 --> 00:07:16.700
The couple had a child and lived a happy life.

00:07:17.330 --> 00:07:21.740
One day, the man heard about a bear that had attacked the villagers..

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.040
He volunteered to take care of that bear.

00:07:30.410 --> 00:07:34.320
Seems like you're working for everyone's happiness.

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:35.780
That is good.

00:07:36.590 --> 00:07:40.460
Oh, isn't that the bear you're looking for?

00:07:41.860 --> 00:07:44.530
Now, shoot for everyone's sake.

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.460
For love's sake. Now.

00:07:56.240 --> 00:07:58.440
No way.

00:07:59.010 --> 00:08:01.040
How could this be?

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.380
Why?

00:08:03.380 --> 00:08:05.180
Why are you here?

00:08:14.390 --> 00:08:15.860
Oh, right.

00:08:15.860 --> 00:08:19.130
By the way, after you left to help everyone,

00:08:19.130 --> 00:08:22.700
your son was apparently eaten by the bear.

00:08:22.700 --> 00:08:26.870
Because of that, that woman was desperately searching for you.

00:08:29.670 --> 00:08:32.540
Such wonderful despair.

00:08:34.180 --> 00:08:36.140
It's wonderfully delicious.

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.450
It was worth waiting all this time.

00:08:38.450 --> 00:08:41.020
This is my delicacy.

00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:44.250
His name is Jasei.

00:08:44.790 --> 00:08:48.060
He's the strongest and worst mage with a cruel spirit.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:52.560
His source of nutrients was human despair.

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:54.400
He would chain together events,

00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:56.600
and destroy their happiness.

00:08:57.200 --> 00:09:00.870
The despair from that moment is his favorite.

00:09:03.910 --> 00:09:05.070
Why?

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:07.180
Because I want to live.

00:09:07.510 --> 00:09:09.610
Because it is fun.

00:09:09.610 --> 00:09:14.080
I love the expression they get when their pure souls are torn to pieces.

00:09:14.080 --> 00:09:18.390
It feels good to turn their expected future right at its base.

00:09:18.390 --> 00:09:22.060
When one is betrayed by something they trusted greatly...

00:09:22.060 --> 00:09:28.030
The grief when they lose something more precious than their own life...

00:09:28.030 --> 00:09:29.900
That's the most delicious thing.

00:09:29.900 --> 00:09:32.500
Wait. The reason you were raising me was...

00:09:32.500 --> 00:09:34.100
That is correct.

00:09:34.100 --> 00:09:39.110
I taught love, justice, and a beautiful heart to your lonely self.

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:43.410
It's so I can taste that pure despair of yours.

00:09:44.610 --> 00:09:46.920
So how does it feel?

00:09:46.920 --> 00:09:51.220
This man you love, respect, and who taught you everything.

00:09:51.220 --> 00:09:54.060
How does it feel to have them denied?

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:58.060
That despair shall be the food for me to live.

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:04.400
I can't cry.

00:10:04.400 --> 00:10:06.470
Rather, I take pity on you.

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:10.310
You're the one who taught me those feelings.

00:10:10.640 --> 00:10:13.680
So you won't even despair from this?

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:20.780
Lastly, let's predict your future.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:24.850
One day the ones you hold dear will go against you.

00:10:24.850 --> 00:10:27.190
They'll throw rocks at you and you'll despair.

00:10:27.190 --> 00:10:31.460
Among that despair, you will disappear from this world.

00:10:31.460 --> 00:10:34.360
That is a fate you cannot avoid.

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:40.070
May you be blessed by an eternal curse.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:57.620
This is me?

00:10:58.150 --> 00:10:59.620
That's right.

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:01.790
That's your real body.

00:11:01.790 --> 00:11:04.990
With my magic, I moved your soul

00:11:04.990 --> 00:11:08.300
and placed it in a fake body.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:12.070
The only one who knows how to return it is me.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:14.700
No.

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:17.110
Writhe. Suffer!

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:19.840
And when you know you cannot turn back,

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:22.880
you will learn what true despair is.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:27.920
But I did not lose hope.

00:11:27.920 --> 00:11:31.090
Ever since then, my fight started.

00:11:34.360 --> 00:11:35.560
"Inukami!"

00:11:35.560 --> 00:11:37.030
Woof woof.

00:11:37.260 --> 00:11:39.960
So the body at the villa.

00:11:39.960 --> 00:11:42.530
That's your real body?

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:46.440
This body is artificial.

00:11:46.440 --> 00:11:51.240
It's a body Jasei made that moves and grows just like the original.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:54.540
But in the end, it's just a fake. Look.

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.380
It's at its end.

00:11:57.950 --> 00:12:01.520
That's why I have to return to my original body as soon as possible.

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:04.820
But I just don't know how.

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:08.620
That's why you planned to borrow Sekidousai's power.

00:12:09.160 --> 00:12:12.660
Nadeshiko, you knew about this for a while?

00:12:13.530 --> 00:12:17.200
Nadeshiko found out by accident.

00:12:17.200 --> 00:12:18.700
Why?

00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:21.070
Why did you keep quiet about it?

00:12:21.070 --> 00:12:24.540
Sure, we can't use magic like Sekidousai.

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:28.140
But the ten of us might have been able to help.

00:12:28.140 --> 00:12:30.180
And yet you kept hiding it.

00:12:30.610 --> 00:12:32.380
I'm sorry, Tayune.

00:12:32.380 --> 00:12:34.220
I had no other choice.

00:12:34.220 --> 00:12:36.220
That was my curse.

00:12:37.420 --> 00:12:40.660
I must not tell anyone about my body.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:43.890
Otherwise, I could never return to my real body.

00:12:43.890 --> 00:12:46.430
That's his last curse.

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:50.770
Then by telling us about it...

00:12:50.770 --> 00:12:53.240
I don't mind anymore.

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:57.270
I was just afraid of losing everyone.

00:12:59.540 --> 00:13:03.450
Nothing happened after Nadeshiko found out.

00:13:03.850 --> 00:13:07.050
Maybe there was no such curse to begin with.

00:13:08.280 --> 00:13:11.990
But as I fought with Keita,
I thought about it.

00:13:12.620 --> 00:13:15.560
What am I fighting for?

00:13:16.360 --> 00:13:20.000
Even if I protected Sekidousai and got my body back,

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:22.200
I would lose everything.

00:13:22.830 --> 00:13:26.070
I realized that would be more painful.

00:13:26.600 --> 00:13:29.870
Even if I lose my body,
I won't lose hope.

00:13:30.670 --> 00:13:33.640
But if I lose everyone,
I couldn't live.

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:38.650
That's why I wanted to tell everyone the truth.

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:41.650
That's everything
I heard from Sekidousai.

00:13:42.120 --> 00:13:46.660
Apparently he used Daisakkai to investigate Kaoru Kawahira's past.

00:13:46.660 --> 00:13:48.790
Oh, that's it?

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:49.860
Keita?

00:13:49.860 --> 00:13:51.730
It's easy, right?

00:13:52.330 --> 00:13:53.330
Yeah.

00:13:58.170 --> 00:14:01.140
Blood of Sekidou, come.

00:14:02.400 --> 00:14:05.110
Purification Barrier, Type 2.
Purple Pillar.

00:14:05.110 --> 00:14:07.880
I call you in the name of Kasan Soukun.

00:14:07.880 --> 00:14:12.950
Flashing lights and darkness.
Combine and destroy everything.

00:14:15.980 --> 00:14:18.490
As expected of the Kawahira head.

00:14:18.490 --> 00:14:20.520
I want your power.

00:14:20.520 --> 00:14:21.760
Mass petrification!

00:14:21.760 --> 00:14:22.790
Look out!

00:14:23.430 --> 00:14:24.560
Hake.

00:14:25.130 --> 00:14:26.030
Got you.

00:14:36.470 --> 00:14:38.610
Yoko, go back to the city.

00:14:39.070 --> 00:14:40.740
Stop Sekidousai.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:42.180
But what about you?

00:14:42.580 --> 00:14:45.380
I don't like it, but I can't fight with this body.

00:14:45.380 --> 00:14:48.650
But I'll catch up with you.
Please hold on until then.

00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:50.690
Got it. I'm going.

00:14:56.390 --> 00:14:58.730
Master Kaoru, where are you going?

00:14:59.060 --> 00:15:01.460
It's my responsibility that this happened.

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:03.570
So I'll defeat Sekidousai.

00:15:04.300 --> 00:15:05.930
Please don't come.

00:15:05.930 --> 00:15:09.370
I can't get you involved in my personal fight.

00:15:09.370 --> 00:15:11.770
And besides, I've deceived you all.

00:15:12.610 --> 00:15:17.280
An Inukami User who vanquishes evil helped an evil mage.

00:15:17.780 --> 00:15:22.380
I no longer have the right to be your master.

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:23.180
Sendan.

00:15:23.180 --> 00:15:23.750
Yes?

00:15:23.750 --> 00:15:26.760
Igusa, Tayune, Gokyoya...

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:29.760
Tensou, Furano, Imari...

00:15:29.760 --> 00:15:31.760
Sayoka, Tomohane...

00:15:31.760 --> 00:15:33.900
And Nadeshiko.

00:15:34.900 --> 00:15:37.830
I'm truly thankful that you all followed me until now.

00:15:41.400 --> 00:15:43.040
What should we do?

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:45.070
I don't know.

00:15:45.070 --> 00:15:46.940
He said so much at once.

00:15:48.440 --> 00:15:51.350
Why are you guys hesitating?

00:15:51.350 --> 00:15:52.650
Yeah, why?

00:15:53.280 --> 00:15:55.280
It's just that Master Kaoru...

00:15:55.280 --> 00:15:57.420
isn't Master Kaoru.

00:16:03.160 --> 00:16:07.460
I never thought the twins would be the ones to speak reasonably.

00:16:07.860 --> 00:16:09.100
You're right.

00:16:09.100 --> 00:16:10.830
Master Kaoru is Master Kaoru.

00:16:10.830 --> 00:16:12.830
Still the same as we know.

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:19.240
Let's go.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:36.320
Look at the brilliance of my 16 cm cannon.

00:16:43.800 --> 00:16:46.370
Goodbye, Kaoru Kawahira.

00:16:51.110 --> 00:16:52.640
Master Kaoru!

00:16:53.010 --> 00:16:54.040
Imari, Sayoka.

00:16:54.040 --> 00:16:57.010
You impudent little...

00:16:57.010 --> 00:16:58.380
Take this!

00:17:04.050 --> 00:17:08.690
Master Kaoru. We, your Inukami, will follow you wherever you go.

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:09.820
Master Kaoru.

00:17:09.820 --> 00:17:10.990
Everyone.

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:17.870
Um, we're...

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:20.370
It's all right.

00:17:20.640 --> 00:17:21.900
Master Kaoru.

00:17:22.300 --> 00:17:23.910
Master Kaoru.

00:17:25.070 --> 00:17:26.980
Thank you, everyone.

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:31.550
Thanks to you, I've found new hope.

00:17:31.550 --> 00:17:34.550
Oh my, how sentimental.

00:17:34.880 --> 00:17:39.320
And what can you do with those pet puppies?

00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:40.960
Sekidousai.

00:17:41.260 --> 00:17:43.860
Don't think I'm the same as before.

00:17:44.430 --> 00:17:46.560
All of my Inukami are here.

00:17:46.560 --> 00:17:49.630
I'm an Inukami User.

00:17:49.630 --> 00:17:51.730
Inukami User?

00:17:52.170 --> 00:17:53.470
Let's go, everyone.

00:17:53.470 --> 00:17:55.440
Yes, Master Kaoru.

00:17:55.840 --> 00:17:58.210
In the name of Tousan Shinkun.

00:17:58.210 --> 00:18:00.810
Atmosphere, sing upon a symphony.

00:18:02.110 --> 00:18:05.480
Blood of Sekidou, come.

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:07.220
Imari. Sayoka.

00:18:09.580 --> 00:18:11.690
Leave the stealing to us.

00:18:14.690 --> 00:18:15.660
What?

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:17.360
Darn you.

00:18:17.690 --> 00:18:19.630
Gokyoya, Tensou, Furano.

00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:28.340
Oh, you're doing good.

00:18:28.340 --> 00:18:30.610
Yoko? Where's Keita?

00:18:30.610 --> 00:18:32.140
He's fine for now.

00:18:32.140 --> 00:18:34.810
I was told to help you guys.

00:18:34.810 --> 00:18:36.310
But you don't need it.

00:18:36.310 --> 00:18:37.350
No, I do.

00:18:37.350 --> 00:18:38.980
Don't you underestimate me.

00:18:42.080 --> 00:18:44.790
It's gone.

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:48.690
I was really happy being Master Kaoru's Inukami.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:49.690
Evil Blaze!

00:18:50.930 --> 00:18:52.960
Everyone was really nice.

00:18:52.960 --> 00:18:55.400
Every day was really fun.

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:58.000
But, what I wanted...

00:18:58.000 --> 00:19:00.770
Darn it! Take this!

00:19:00.770 --> 00:19:01.340
The only thing I wanted was a secret between Master Kaoru and me.

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:02.670
Purple Pillar!

00:19:02.670 --> 00:19:03.970
But I no longer have it. It's gone.

00:19:03.970 --> 00:19:05.410
Crimson!

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:06.710
But I no longer have it. It's gone.

00:19:09.710 --> 00:19:14.180
Mere beasts.
You dare to gang up on me?

00:19:14.180 --> 00:19:16.150
Daisakkai.

00:19:25.430 --> 00:19:31.500
With Dai Yoko, Blood of Sekidou, and the maxed out Daisakkai...

00:19:31.500 --> 00:19:33.470
I am invincible!

00:19:33.800 --> 00:19:35.140
I won't let you.

00:19:35.140 --> 00:19:35.840
Everyone!

00:19:35.840 --> 00:19:36.800
Yes!

00:19:37.370 --> 00:19:38.940
Evil Blaze.

00:19:38.940 --> 00:19:42.910
Purification Flash.
Manifestation x9. Purgatory.

00:19:48.120 --> 00:19:50.350
Darn you, Kaoru Kawahira.

00:19:58.330 --> 00:20:00.930
So this is Dai Yoko's power.

00:20:03.700 --> 00:20:06.530
Nadeshiko, go to Daisakkai.

00:20:06.940 --> 00:20:10.640
With its current power, any wish will come true.

00:20:10.640 --> 00:20:13.780
Wish so that the Dai Yoko doll would be powerless.

00:20:13.780 --> 00:20:15.380
Hurry up.

00:20:15.380 --> 00:20:16.810
Yes.

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:18.710
Not a chance.

00:20:18.710 --> 00:20:20.350
Never!

00:20:22.250 --> 00:20:23.720
Nadeshiko, hurry.

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:25.250
Nadeshiko.

00:20:25.250 --> 00:20:27.460
Hurry. We can't hold it any longer.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:38.530
If I use this, I can grant any wish.

00:20:39.770 --> 00:20:52.050
My wish is...

00:20:59.350 --> 00:21:00.890
Nadeshiko.

00:21:04.290 --> 00:21:06.790
Master Kaoru.

00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:14.840
Nadeshiko.

00:21:14.840 --> 00:21:16.570
No.

00:21:16.570 --> 00:21:18.970
So this is your despair.

00:21:20.640 --> 00:21:23.750
I'm satisfied, Kaoru Kawahira.

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:43.100
<i>This and that, we want everything</i>

00:21:43.100 --> 00:21:48.470
<i>We wish for love and that all</i> <i>of our dreams will come true</i>

00:21:48.470 --> 00:21:53.610
<i>Every girl is busy</i>

00:21:53.610 --> 00:21:58.810
<i>Playing, studying, going crazy</i>
<i>Our schedules are filled</i>

00:21:59.410 --> 00:22:01.920
<i>When we are about to be dumped,</i>

00:22:01.920 --> 00:22:04.490
<i>we send texts and gather</i>

00:22:04.490 --> 00:22:07.290
<i>A meeting at a family restaurant,</i>

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:10.760
<i>and nothing makes any sense</i>

00:22:11.130 --> 00:22:13.630
<i>Oh, no. Oh, no. Oh, no</i>

00:22:13.630 --> 00:22:16.360
<i>We eat some sweets while we chat</i>

00:22:16.360 --> 00:22:21.570
<i>We can't stop, and now</i> <i>our diets are doomed too</i>

00:22:21.570 --> 00:22:24.040
<i>Oh, no. Oh, no. Oh, no</i>

00:22:24.040 --> 00:22:26.740
<i>When we go crazy together,</i>

00:22:26.740 --> 00:22:32.880
<i>we get so excited that we can</i> <i>forget our sadness a bit</i>

00:22:33.250 --> 00:22:35.620
<i>Let's go. Let's go. Fight</i>

00:22:35.620 --> 00:22:38.350
<i>Our hearts are one,</i>

00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:41.960
<i>tied by a strong bond</i> <i>called friendship</i>

00:22:50.400 --> 00:22:54.040
Inukami!

00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:54.940
See you!

00:22:55.640 --> 00:22:57.240
Her mind is broken...

00:22:57.240 --> 00:23:01.140
With the loss of her loved one, the girl returns to her old self.

00:23:01.140 --> 00:23:04.880
The town is reduced to rubble.
The lively voices are lost.

00:23:04.880 --> 00:23:07.850
Nothing can be heard nor reached.

00:23:07.850 --> 00:23:12.020
Towards the single worst scenario that only one person wished for,

00:23:12.020 --> 00:23:14.190
everything is turning into ashes.

00:23:15.090 --> 00:23:16.260
Next on Inukami!

00:23:17.020 --> 00:23:18.890
"Banquet of Despair!"

00:23:19.290 --> 00:23:20.030
Darkness covers everything and despair fills everything.

00:23:20.030 --> 00:23:25.000
Banquet of Despair!
